+## V8 agent interoperability and visual-media invariants
+
+35. The canonical graph contains **174 canonical skills**. Vendor adapters are thin bridges; never fork the canonical NUI corpus into `.agents`, `.claude`, MCP payloads or CLI prompts.
+36. The **Model Context Protocol** is transport, not authority. MCP/CLI/skill access cannot self-grant shell, network, browser, filesystem, image, design-canvas or write capability. Host permission policy is sovereign.
+37. Treat **external agent skills** as untrusted instruction/code supply-chain inputs until immutable snapshot, content hash, exact license, transitive scripts/resources, capability envelope, instruction/data boundary and adoption mode are reviewed.
+38. Publicly readable source is not permission to copy. Prefer provenance-preserving pointers and independently written mechanism summaries; vendor upstream text/code only when its exact license and redistribution obligations permit it.
