+The current v8 graph declares **174 canonical skills** spanning the v2 industry cognition system, v3 product closure, v4 ecosystem intelligence, v5 affective/aesthetic enforcement, v6 deep research/design synthesis, v7 Concrete Craft & Authority Intelligence, and v8 Agent Interoperability & Visual Media Intelligence. That number is descriptive, not a target. The router normally loads the **smallest sufficient graph** for the current task; high visual ambition is an explicit exception where required visual faculties become a hard route rather than optional context.
 
 NUI does not promise objective beauty, automatic compliance, or permanent completeness. It constrains observable agent behavior so material assumptions become explicit, high-impact domains cannot be silently omitted, independent critics can falsify the design, machine-checkable invariants are enforced by code, and release claims remain bounded by actual evidence.
 
@@ -161,3 +161,14 @@ For transfer from external products and galleries, the rule is **mechanism, not
 For flagship/exceptional/experiential work, v7 adds a rendered perception gate over the inherited v5 aesthetic gate. A screenshot is not evidence by itself: the record must observe attention hierarchy, resolved typography, subject-linked signature, material roles, responsive recomposition and—when material—temporal sequencing. Reference comparison and critique must identify a weakness, record a fix and verify the changed artifact. Optional pixel-diff evidence is renderer/environment scoped with calibrated tolerance so antialiasing noise is not mistaken for a meaningful visual regression.
 
 See `docs/V7-CONCRETE-KNOWLEDGE-CLOSURE.md` for the critique-to-mechanism closure map and `docs/research/UI-AUTHORITY-INTELLIGENCE-V7.md` for research/transfer boundaries.
+
+
+## Agent Interoperability & Visual Media Intelligence (v8)
+
+NUI v8 exposes the same **174 canonical skills** to Codex, Claude Code, Google Antigravity and other hosts without cloning the canonical graph. Codex/Antigravity use a thin `.agents/skills/nolane-ui` bridge; Claude Code gets `.claude/skills/nolane-ui`; any MCP-capable host can use the bounded local **Model Context Protocol** server; generic agents can use the CLI. Host permission/sandbox settings always remain authoritative.
+
+External agent skills are treated as untrusted supply-chain inputs. A public skill is not automatically safe or copyable: material use requires immutable revision, content hash, per-skill license evidence, executable/capability review, instruction/data quarantine and a bounded adoption mode. NUI defaults to pointers or independently written mechanism summaries rather than bulk-copying upstream prompt prose.
+
+V8 also adds a media decision spine. It does **not** ban geometric UI. It detects **shape substitution**—generic cards/orbs/blobs/fake graphs standing in for real subject matter or evidence—and asks whether photography, archival material, truthful data/diagram, illustration, 3D or generated media would carry more information. External media crosses a strict discovery→use boundary and requires **asset-level rights**/provenance rather than trusting a site's general reputation.
+
+Creative tools are stage authorities, not product authorities. Image generation/editing, Figma, Blender, SVG/Canvas/Three/R3F/Pixi and motion runtimes can be routed for the job they actually perform. Final assets must return to rendered responsive states and pass semantic fit, crop, contrast, performance, accessibility and rights lineage checks.
